BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Sacred Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In ancient times, there was a hidden spring whose waters held a peculiar magic. When a travele) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    r offered water from their flask to the spring, it would triple in volume, but only another ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    person could draw it out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  Two wanderers, the Giver and the Keeper, discovered this spring on the same day. The Giver car) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ried a precious flask, refilled each dawn with five measures of water. The Keeper carried an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (     empty vessel but possessed the strength to draw from the deep spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  At first, the Giver hesitated. "If I pour my water in, the Keeper might take it all and leave ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    me with nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  But the spring whispered: "Trust creates abundance. Hoarding creates scarcity.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The Giver poured three measures into the spring. It became nine. The Keeper drew it out and sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    w the Giver's thirst. Remembering their own thirst, the Keeper returned five measures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  Both drank deeply that day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  They returned each dawn, sometimes as Giver, sometimes as Keeper. They learned that generosity) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     multiplied, that fair return sustained trust, and that together they could transform scarci) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ty into plenty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  The spring still flows, waiting for those wise enough to understand: what is shared grows, wha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    t is hoarded diminishes, and trust rewards the trusting.) Tj ET
