BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  In the time before time, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (     River of Return. Each was controlled by a spirit: Sender, who dwelled upstream, and Receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    r, who lived below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  Sender discovered a magical property: any water released downstream would triple in volume by ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    the time it reached Receiver's domain. But Sender feared: "If I send my waters, will anythin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    g flow back to sustain me?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  So Sender sent only a trickle. It tripled, yes, but Receiver, seeing so little trust, returned) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (     nothing. Both rivers ran dry, and the valley remained barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  One season, Sender took courage and released a generous flow. The waters tripled magnificently) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    , filling Receiver's pools with abundance. Receiver, moved by this trust, sent back a genero) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    us portion upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  Sender's basin was replenished, and there was enough to give again. Each cycle of giving and r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    eturning made their waters stronger. The valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  The spirits learned: the multiplication of gifts only creates abundance when trust flows both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ways. The one who gives first takes the greatest risk, but also opens the possibility of pro) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    sperity. The one who receives holds the power to sustain or destroy that trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  And so the rivers flowed forever after.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
