BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  # The Spring of Abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages lay on opposite sides of a sacred spring. The spring had a myst) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    erious property: any water poured into it from one side would flow to the other side tripled) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (     in volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  The First Village discovered this magic. Their elder, wise in the ways of scarcity, feared: "I) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    f we pour our water into the spring, we give away what is ours. What if the Other Village ke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    eps it all?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  So they poured nothing, and received nothing in return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  But one day, a young villager named Briar stepped forward. "I will trust," she said, and poure) Tj ET
