BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      In ancient times, there was a hidden spring whose waters held a peculiar magic. When a tra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        veler offered water from their flask to the spring, it would triple in volume, but only ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        another person could draw it out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      Two wanderers, the Giver and the Keeper, discovered this spring on the same day. The Giver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         carried a precious flask, refilled each dawn with five measures of water. The Keeper ca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        rried an empty vessel but possessed the strength to draw from the deep spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      At first, the Giver hesitated. "If I pour my water in, the Keeper might take it all and le) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        ave me with nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      But the spring whispered: "Trust creates abundance. Hoarding creates scarcity.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      The Giver poured three measures into the spring. It became nine. The Keeper drew it out an) Tj ET
