BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      In the time before time, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (         the River of Return. Each was controlled by a spirit: Sender, who dwelled upstream, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         Receiver, who lived below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      Sender discovered a magical property: any water released downstream would triple in volume) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         by the time it reached Receiver's domain. But Sender feared: "If I send my waters, will) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (         anything flow back to sustain me?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      So Sender sent only a trickle. It tripled, yes, but Receiver, seeing so little trust, retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        rned nothing. Both rivers ran dry, and the valley remained barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      One season, Sender took courage and released a generous flow. The waters tripled magnifice) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ntly, filling Receiver's pools with abundance. Receiver, moved by this trust, sent back ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        a generous portion upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
