BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a vast desert. Each possessed a magical we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ll that could multiply whatever was poured into it threefold, but the wells had a peculiar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (       enchantment: one village's well could only be filled by water from the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    During the first great drought, the Northern village faced a choice. They could hoard their ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      precious water or send it across the desert, trusting it would return. Elder Hana spoke: ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      True abundance flows like water in a circle, not gold locked in a vault.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    They sent half their reserves. The Southern village received triple the amount, their well o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      verflowing. Grateful and moved by such trust, they returned more than the North had origin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ally sent, keeping enough for their own needs but honoring the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    Season after season, both villages prospered. When either sent generously, the other returne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      d fairly. The desert bloomed with their shared abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    But when fear took root and gifts became miserly, returns grew small too. The wells still mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ltiplied, but the cycle weakened.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    The villages learned: trust creates wealth that hoarding destroys. The magic was never in th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      e wells alone, but in the courage to give and the honor to reciprocate.) Tj ET
