BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        another person could draw it out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      Two wanderers, the Giver and the Keeper, discovered this spring on the same day. The Giver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         carried a precious flask, refilled each dawn with five measures of water. The Keeper ca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        rried an empty vessel but possessed the strength to draw from the deep spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      At first, the Giver hesitated. "If I pour my water in, the Keeper might take it all and le) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ave me with nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      But the spring whispered: "Trust creates abundance. Hoarding creates scarcity.") Tj ET
