BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a vast desert. Each possessed a magical ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        well that could multiply whatever was poured into it threefold, but the wells had a pecu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        liar enchantment: one village's well could only be filled by water from the other villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        e.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      During the first great drought, the Northern village faced a choice. They could hoard thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        r precious water or send it across the desert, trusting it would return. Elder Hana spok) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        e: "True abundance flows like water in a circle, not gold locked in a vault.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      They sent half their reserves. The Southern village received triple the amount, their well) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         overflowing. Grateful and moved by such trust, they returned more than the North had or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        iginally sent, keeping enough for their own needs but honoring the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      Season after season, both villages prospered. When either sent generously, the other retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        ned fairly. The desert bloomed with their shared abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      But when fear took root and gifts became miserly, returns grew small too. The wells still ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        multiplied, but the cycle weakened.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      The villages learned: trust creates wealth that hoarding destroys. The magic was never in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        the wells alone, but in the courage to give and the honor to reciprocate.) Tj ET
