BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a vast desert. Each possessed a magical ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        well that could multiply whatever was poured into it threefold, but the wells had a pecu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        liar enchantment: one village's well could only be filled by water from the other villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        e.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      During the first great drought, the Northern village faced a choice. They could hoard thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        r precious water or send it across the desert, trusting it would return. Elder Hana spok) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        e: "True abundance flows like water in a circle, not gold locked in a vault.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      They sent half their reserves. The Southern village received triple the amount, their well) Tj ET
