BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      In ancient times, two rivers flowed down from separate mountains-the River of Giving and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        he River of Return. Each was fed by a different god, and between them lay a parched vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        ey where mortals struggled.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      One day, a traveler named Theon stood at the River of Giving. The god spoke: "Whatever wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        er you pour into the valley, I shall triple." But Theon feared losing what little he had) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      Across the valley, another traveler, Kara, watched. She called out: "Send your waters! I v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ow to return half of what flows to me, so both our vessels shall overflow.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      Theon, trusting her word, poured his full vessel. The god tripled it, and the valley bloom) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        ed green. Kara received abundance and, true to her word, returned half. Both travelers f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        ound themselves with more than they began.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      The gods smiled and spoke as one: "When Givers trust and Receivers honor, all thirsts are ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        quenched. But when either breaks faith-when Givers hoard or Receivers keep all-the valle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        y remains dust.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
