BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      In ancient times, there was a hidden spring whose waters held a peculiar magic. When a tra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        veler offered water from their flask to the spring, it would triple in volume, but only ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        another person could draw it out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      Two wanderers, the Giver and the Keeper, discovered this spring on the same day. The Giver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (         carried a precious flask, refilled each dawn with five measures of water. The Keeper ca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        rried an empty vessel but possessed the strength to draw from the deep spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
