BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood separated by a vast desert. Each possessed a magical ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        well that could multiply whatever was poured into it threefold, but the wells had a pecu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        liar enchantment: one village's well could only be filled by water from the other villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        e.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      During the first great drought, the Northern village faced a choice. They could hoard thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        r precious water or send it across the desert, trusting it would return. Elder Hana spok) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        e: "True abundance flows like water in a circle, not gold locked in a vault.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      They sent half their reserves. The Southern village received triple the amount, their well) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (         overflowing. Grateful and moved by such trust, they returned more than the North had or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        iginally sent, keeping enough for their own needs but honoring the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      Season after season, both villages prospered. When either sent generously, the other retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        ned fairly. The desert bloomed with their shared abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      But when fear took root and gifts became miserly, returns grew small too. The wells still ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        multiplied, but the cycle weakened.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      The villages learned: trust creates wealth that hoarding destroys. The magic was never in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        the wells alone, but in the courage to give and the honor to reciprocate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      In the beginning, there were two rivers: the River of Giving and the River of Returning. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        ach flowed from a different mountain, never meeting, never mingling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The River of Giving was blessed by the Sun God, who each dawn placed five golden drops int) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        o its source. The river could choose to send these drops downstream or keep them in its ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        pools. When drops traveled downstream, they multiplied threefold by the time they reache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        d the valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      The River of Returning dwelt in that valley, receiving whatever the River of Giving sent. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        Upon receiving the multiplied waters, the River of Returning faced a choice: to hold the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (         abundance or send some back upstream to its benefactor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      For many seasons, both rivers were cautious. The River of Giving sent little, fearing loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        . The River of Returning kept much, fearing scarcity. Both remained shallow and weak.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Then came a drought. In desperation, the River of Giving poured forth all five drops in tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ust. The threefold waters revived the River of Returning, who gratefully sent half back ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        upstream. Both rivers swelled with abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      From that day forward, the rivers understood: trust multiplies blessings, and reciprocity ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        creates plenty. When both give generously, both flow abundantly. This is the eternal tru) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        th of the Twin Rivers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
