BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      Myth: In the dawn age, two spirits tended a mystical garden-the Planter and the Harvester.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (         The Planter received five seeds each morning. Any seed planted would grow into a tree b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        earing three times its fruit, but only the Harvester could gather it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      For many seasons, fear ruled them. The Planter hoarded seeds, planting few. The Harvester,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         finding meager harvests, returned nothing. The garden withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      One morning, the Planter planted three seeds with trembling hands-more than half their dai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        ly gift. By evening, nine golden fruits hung heavy on the branches. The Harvester stood ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        at a crossroads: take all and feast alone, or honor the Planter's courage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The Harvester remembered their own hunger during the barren seasons. They returned five fr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        uits to the Planter, who now held seven-more than they started with. The Harvester kept ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        four, abundance neither had known before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The next day, trust made the Planter bold again. The Harvester's fairness made returning n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        atural. The garden flourished into paradise.) Tj ET
