BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      In ancient times, the goddess Elara discovered a silver river that flowed between two vill) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        ages. The river possessed a miraculous quality: any gift cast into its waters would trip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        le before reaching the opposite shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      The first village elder, hesitant and fearful, tossed only a single copper coin into the c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        urrent. It became three on the far bank. The receiving village, grateful but cautious, r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        eturned one coin. Both villages remained as they were-surviving, but not thriving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      Then a young weaver approached the river. She had only five threads of silk, all she owned) Tj ET
