BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      In the beginning, there were two rivers: the River of Giving and the River of Returning. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ach flowed from a different mountain, never meeting, never mingling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      The River of Giving was blessed by the Sun God, who each dawn placed five golden drops int) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        o its source. The river could choose to send these drops downstream or keep them in its ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        pools. When drops traveled downstream, they multiplied threefold by the time they reache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        d the valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      The River of Returning dwelt in that valley, receiving whatever the River of Giving sent. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        Upon receiving the multiplied waters, the River of Returning faced a choice: to hold the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (         abundance or send some back upstream to its benefactor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      For many seasons, both rivers were cautious. The River of Giving sent little, fearing loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        . The River of Returning kept much, fearing scarcity. Both remained shallow and weak.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      Then came a drought. In desperation, the River of Giving poured forth all five drops in tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        ust. The threefold waters revived the River of Returning, who gratefully sent half back ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        upstream. Both rivers swelled with abundance.) Tj ET
