BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      She told of two weavers who found the silver river. The first weaver, remembering ancient ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        wisdom, cast three of her five threads downstream with open heart. They became nine. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (         receiving village, seeing her courage, honored it by returning six threads-keeping thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        e for their own looms. The weaver gained eight threads; the village gained three. Both p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        rospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      The second weaver, consumed by fear, sent only one thread. It became three, but the receiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        ers, seeing such timid faith, returned merely one. Both remained trapped in scarcity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      "But what," asked the apprentice, "if the receiving village keeps all nine threads?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      Elara's eyes grew dark. "Then the river reveals truth. The generous weaver learns whom to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        trust and whom to avoid. The greedy village may feast once, but word spreads. Soon no th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        reads flow their way, and their looms fall silent.") Tj ET
