BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      For many seasons, fear ruled them. The Planter hoarded seeds, planting few. The Harvester,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (         finding meager harvests, returned nothing. The garden withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      One morning, the Planter planted three seeds with trembling hands-more than half their dai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        ly gift. By evening, nine golden fruits hung heavy on the branches. The Harvester stood ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        at a crossroads: take all and feast alone, or honor the Planter's courage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
