BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        ng all her water in hope.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      The water flowed across, tripled, to Galen the shepherd on the far side. He stood amazed a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        t this unexpected gift-fifteen measures where there had been nothing! His flocks drank d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        eep, and he pondered: should he keep this windfall or honor the trust shown to him?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      Galen remembered the old teaching: "A gift tripled is meant to be shared, not hoarded." He) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         returned seven measures-less than half, yet more than Briar's original five. Both prosp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        ered from this exchange.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      As seasons turned, Briar and Galen learned the spring's true rhythm. Sometimes Galen poure) Tj ET
